Active Storybound UI artwork
---------------------------
The document icons in ui-kit/concepts/documents/*-16.png and the matching
game textures are extracted from the user-supplied approved sheet
ui-kit/assets/image.png. The source hash, crop rectangles and sampling
rules are recorded in items16.json and build-icons.ps1. Earlier manually
reconstructed variants were superseded. The book silhouette follows the
vanilla Minecraft book; Minecraft-derived elements are not claimed as
original Storybound intellectual property or relicensed under GPL.
Minecraft content belongs to Mojang/Microsoft. No Pngtree or PIXTA files
or third-party resource-pack icon files are included. See
docs/ui-kit/documents.md for provenance and extraction details.

textures/gui/journal/vanilla_book.png and traveler_corner.png are original
assets generated for Storybound using the built-in OpenAI imagegen tool.
Refinements used the project's own artwork. No third-party reference pixels
were imported. The book's accepted material includes red leather, brass
fittings, printed parchment ornaments and restrained dithering.

textures/gui/document/book_leather.png is an original reading-book texture
generated with the built-in imagegen tool. References were the project's
own Adventure Menu background and item contact sheet. The reading version
uses muted red leather and new printed angular ornaments without tabs,
metal corners or protruding sheets. See docs/ui-kit/documents.md.

textures/gui/document/scroll.png is a parchment-scroll reading texture
generated with the built-in imagegen tool, using the project's current
book texture and the user-approved item sheet as references. Its paper
rolls, small printed ornaments and red tie are separate from live text.
No third-party resource-pack textures or game artwork were imported.

textures/gui/document/parchment.png is a letter-in-envelope reading texture
generated with the built-in imagegen tool from the approved project mockup,
followed by a silhouette-cleanup edit. The original letter used the accepted
project scroll texture and user-approved item sheet as material references.
It includes quiet paper, small printed corners, a folded corner, a dithered
contact shadow and a lower-right wax seal on the envelope. No Pngtree pixels
were imported. All letter text is rendered live from existing document content.

textures/gui/document/note.png is an original note reading texture generated
with the built-in imagegen tool. The initial references were the approved
project item sheet and current letter material. A subsequent edit of that
project texture replaces the turned corner with two offset cream notes and
sparse edge dithering. The plain rear sheet extends to the right; the
intermediate third layer and rear-sheet ink sketch were removed on review.
All main-sheet note text is live. No external reference artwork was imported.
The previous note_torn style remains available for explicit legacy overrides.

textures/gui/document/contract.png is an original contract reading texture
generated with the built-in imagegen tool. References were the approved
project inventory sheet's fifth item and the current note material.
It uses cream paper rolls, restrained brown side marks, sparse dithering
and a crimson lower-right wax seal with short ribbons. Text, conditions,
reward and hint remain live content. No external artwork was imported.

BookmarkPixels, JournalSkin and ArchiveChrome draw original pixel emblems,
cloth ribbons, reward glints, an XP orb, printed rules and button frames.
The SVG icon sheet in ui-kit is a mechanical export of those same emblems.
No Minecraft item textures are bundled as UI icons.

Fonts
-----
The active Adventure Menu font is minecraft:default, resolved at runtime.
Minecraft font files are not copied into this repository or the mod jar.
Resource packs may replace the runtime font. The retired journal font ids
remain as aliases to minecraft:default. The separate document font aliases
minecraft:uniform. Experimental font binaries and their conversion tools
were removed during UI kit cleanup on 2026-10-26.

Reference policy
----------------
No assets from Excalibur, Pixel Perfection, Relics, The Witcher, Diablo IV,
Stardew Valley, Craftpix or the supplied reference images are distributed.
New external materials require source-specific license review before import.
Client screenshots in ui-kit illustrate the implementation in Minecraft;
they are not a standalone redistribution of Mojang fonts or game assets.

See docs/ui-kit/graphics.md and docs/ui-kit/cleanup.md for the active inventory and
retired experiment manifest. Storybound source and original project assets
are distributed under the repository's GPL-3.0-only license.
